          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Just as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model-categorical
            version of an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %em Quillen adjoint triple
            should be a model-categorical version of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
          %p
            However, there are various levels of generality at which this could be defined. The simplest would be an adjoint triple between model categories in which both adjunctions are Quillen adjunctions. However, this would require the middle functor to be both Quillen left adjoint and Quillen right adjoint for the same model structures, which (though not impossible) is a strong restriction. A more general notion is obtained by allowing the model structures on one or both of the categories to vary between the two Quillen adjunctions, but keeping the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            type so that when we pass to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            or derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-categories
            we still get an adjoint triple (such as in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2Ho%28CombModCat%29"} 2Ho(CombModCat)
          %p
            Currently, this page is primarily about a very restrictive case where only one of the model structures is allowed to vary, and the Quillen equivalence between the two model structures on that side must be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
          %h2#definition Definition
          #QuillenAdjointTriple.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Quillen adjoint triple)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1, \mathcal{C}_2, \mathcal{D}
              be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_2
              share the same underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            #eq:EquivForQuillenAdjointTriple.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 2
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi Qu
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mi id
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                          %mi id
                          %mphantom
                            %mi AA
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_2
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{ \phantom{AA}id\phantom{AA} }{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{ \phantom{AA}id\phantom{AA} }{\longleftarrow}}
                    {{}_{\phantom{Qu}}\simeq_{Qu}}
                    \\mathcal{C}_1
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjoint+triple"} Quillen adjoint triple
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 1
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi Qu
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mi Qu
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_1
                    \\underoverset
                    {{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {{}_{\phantom{Qu}}\bot_{Qu}}
                    \\mathcal{D}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mn 2
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi Qu
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi C
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_2
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{C}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {{}_{\phantom{Qu}}\bot_{Qu}}
                    \\mathcal{D}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunctions"} Quillen adjunctions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category+of+model+categories"} double category of model categories
            #eq:Comparison2MorphismForQuillenAdjointTriple.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒟
                          %mtd
